    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0326" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg220"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-30">August 30,
                        1906</date>.</hi></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 177.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 353, of the 18th ultimo, transmitting correspondence with the
                    consul-general at Hankow in regard to the regulations for governing the
                    commercial settlement of Changteh Fu, in Honan, and your objections to some of
                    them, and to inform you that your objections commend themselves to the
                    department and are in accord with its telegram of May 8 last, directing that in
                    discussing regulations for international settlements at Antung and Mukden the
                    American agent object to irksome Chinese supervision and arbitrary municipal
                    regulations.</p>
                <p>If Americans are to secure proper treatment at Mukden and Antung, the best way to
                    do so is to begin by insisting in every case that regulations which may become a
                    precedent for future ports shall contain no objectionable features.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
